<Base title="Get Involved: Learn, Code & Collaborate | det.io" description="Get involved with DET.io: study open research, contribute Apache 2.0 code, discuss AI and infrastructure collaboration, or prepare as an operator." path="/participate" pageType="CollectionPage" breadcrumbs={[{name:"Home",href:"/"},{name:"Get involved",href:"/participate"}]}>
<div class="container-site"><div class="editorial-hero"><p class="folio">GET INVOLVED</p><h1>Start with your curiosity.<br/>Contribute what you know.</h1><p class="intro">There are practical ways to engage with the Foundation’s work today. Choose the path that matches your interest, whether you are exploring an idea or bringing specialist experience.</p></div>
<nav class="path-tabs" aria-label="Participation paths"><a href="#learn">I want to learn</a><a href="#contribute">I want to contribute</a><a href="#collaborate">I want to collaborate</a><a href="#operators">I run infrastructure</a></nav>
<section class="editorial-section" id="learn"><p class="folio">01 / LEARNERS &amp; RESEARCHERS</p><div><h2>Follow an idea through to its evidence.</h2><p>Start with a question you want to understand. How does a cloud marketplace allocate resources? What information does an identity check reveal? How could an autonomous agent remain subject to human oversight?</p><ol><li>Choose a question in the research portfolio or an introductory VirtEngine guide.</li><li>Read the linked program explanation, then inspect the technical documentation or source.</li><li>Compare the intended design with its stated development status. Send a clear question or suggest an improvement if an explanation is missing.</li></ol><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-button" href="/research">Choose a research topic →</a><a class="foundation-link" href="https://virtengine.com/learn/how-the-marketplace-works">Start with the marketplace guide ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section" id="contribute"><p class="folio">02 / DEVELOPERS &amp; WRITERS</p><div><h2>Make the next contribution useful.</h2><p>Open-source work benefits from clear explanations, tests, issue reports, and careful review as well as code. VirtEngine and Bosun publish their implementations under Apache 2.0.</p><ol><li>Choose the relevant repository and read its current README and contribution instructions.</li><li>Check existing issues. For a bug, include the version, reproduction steps, expected behaviour, and observed result.</li><li>Discuss a substantial proposed change before implementing it. Follow the repository’s security reporting process for vulnerabilities.</li></ol><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-button" href="https://github.com/virtengine/virtengine">VirtEngine source ↗</a><a class="foundation-link" href="https://github.com/virtengine/bosun">Bosun source ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section" id="collaborate"><p class="folio">03 / RESEARCH COLLABORATION</p><div><h2>Bring a question with a public purpose.</h2><p>We welcome enquiries concerning privacy, distributed infrastructure, technology education, and accountable AI. A useful starting point is a defined problem and an explanation of who could benefit from addressing it.</p><ol><li>Identify the program or research question your enquiry relates to.</li><li>Describe your background, the proposed work, and any relevant public code or publications.</li><li>Explain the intended public benefit and practical constraints. Avoid sending sensitive personal or confidential research data in an initial enquiry.</li></ol><p>Contact opens a discussion. It does not establish a partnership, funding commitment, or program place.</p><a class="foundation-button" href="mailto:hello@det.io?subject=Research%20collaboration">Discuss a research question ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section" id="operators"><p class="folio">04 / INFRASTRUCTURE OPERATORS</p><div><h2>Understand the requirements before participating.</h2><p>VirtEngine’s operator material explains the proposed provider and validator roles. The network is not live, so those pages support learning and preparation rather than access to an available earning opportunity.</p><ol><li>Check the official network status and launch conditions.</li><li>Review the architecture, integration requirements, key management, and security responsibilities.</li><li>Use official release and verification instructions when a network becomes available.</li></ol><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-button" href="https://virtengine.com/providers">Review provider requirements ↗</a><a class="foundation-link" href="https://virtengine.com/network">Check network status ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section"><p class="folio">FOUNDATION MEMBERSHIP</p><div><h2>Contribution and membership are different.</h2><p>Reading resources and contributing to open-source projects do not require formal Foundation membership. Membership is a constitutional role with eligibility rules, limited places, and an approval process.</p><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-link" href="/foundation/membership">Read the membership explanation →</a><a class="foundation-link" href="/contact">Contact the Foundation →</a></div></div></section></div>
